60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,Candidate A uses greenhouses. Candidate B uses animals. Candidate C uses spectroscopy. Candidate D uses field sites.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate A needs phenotyping technicians, which we lack. Candidate C needs modelling, which is seconded.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Candidate C relies on the spectroscopy suite, which was idle for eleven weeks. That is a red flag.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate C benefits from free simulation hours. Candidate B faces high animal day rates.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Candidate D relies on field sites, which have been hit by flooding. Candidate A is indoor but glasshouses are full.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, if field sites are unstable, Candidate D is risky. But the repository is fast.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Victoria, if the spectroscopy suite is unreliable, Candidate C is at risk. But the modelling gap is also a problem.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Ryuji, the animal facility is stable, but the cost is high. Candidate B is viable but expensive.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, Candidate A is indoor, avoiding field risks, but the glasshouse capacity is tight.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, the glasshouse subsidy helps, but the booking is solid. Candidate A might face delays.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"Candidate D produces a catalogue, which the closeout files show endures. The field risk is high, but the data value is high.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate C has the modelling gap and the spectroscopy risk. It seems the most fragile.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"Candidate B is stable in terms of facility accreditation, but the cost and the breeding colony overrun risk are concerns.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate A has the glasshouse capacity issue, but the cost is manageable due to the subsidy.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"Candidate D has the field risk, but the repository turnaround is excellent. The metadata standardization is a plus.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I am leaning towards Candidate D for its long-term value, despite the field risks.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I am concerned about Candidate C's reliance on unavailable staff and unstable equipment.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I am wary of Candidate C's instrumentation risk. Candidate B is a safer bet, though costly.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate A is a balanced choice, with manageable costs and indoor stability.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I think Candidate D offers the most robust data infrastructure, even with the field challenges.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
